  "record": {
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "Fixed the FF8 Character surface as a panel-level rule. The color mismatch came from restarting the same gradient on three nested elements: the physical toolbar, selector container, and portrait list. The selector and portrait list are now transparent, so only the outer framed panel draws the surface. I also removed FF8 detail-field subdivision borders, made the three Limit Break fields fill the row through its right edge, and kept each type rail inside its field track. The full FF8 rendered UI suite passes.",
